            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Caroline C"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I added a splash of my favorite white balsamic vinegar to the vinaigrette. Also, common sense dictates you toast the bagel first. Raw bagels are nasty!"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "cmach"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I am presently enjoying this delightful sandwich! I didn’t have arugula so made it with spinach and as the grocery store radishes are huge , I just used 1. Also, since I had white balsamic vinegar, I used a splash as another viewer suggested. This is a great sandwich adaptable to what you have on hand!",
            "datePublished": "2023-07-03T20:32:34.694Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "3"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "France C"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I was a little disappointed in this. I was expecting bright, fresh flavors due to the radish, cream cheese and arugula, but the sandwich was quite bland. I made it exactly as written and thought 1/4 cup of cream cheese was way too much. You could easily get away with using half that. The sandwich was also messy and hard to eat due to the layer of radishes, which caused everything to slide around with each bite. I probably would have preferred a toasted bagel, as others have mentioned. Store-bought flavored cream cheese would have been easier and more flavorful.",
            "datePublished": "2023-04-30T20:56:43.332Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "LindaB2Lost"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Yes, I made some changes. I used some on hand ingredients. I used balsamic vinegar instead of vinaigrette and Sandwich Thins instead of bagels. Someone else substituted cucumbers for the radishes, so I used both! Good! Made it a second time with more generous spread of cream cheese and substituted sandwich pickles for some of the cucumbers. Will make again.",
            "datePublished": "2015-09-30T14:32:21.690Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
